{"id":"7b38a86167a27aab0e011dffc0a7a4729bb3d447","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"7b38a86167a27aab0e011dffc0a7a4729bb3d447","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/pnpr-container-shutdown-readiness.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/pnpr\": minor","+---","+","+pnpr now responds to Unix `SIGTERM` signals with graceful shutdown, stopping new connections and completing in-flight requests before exiting. Dedicated readiness (`/-/ready`) and liveness (`/-/live`) endpoints are now available for container orchestration, and `/-/ping` returns 503 when backend storage or auth is inaccessible [pnpm/tasks#131](https://github.com/pnpm/tasks/issues/131)."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/auth/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -169,6 +169,13 @@ impl AuthState {","         Self { users, tokens: Arc::new(tokens) }","     }"," ","+    /// Check that the auth backends (users and tokens) are reachable and ready.","+    pub async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        self.users.check_readiness().await?;","+        self.tokens.check_readiness().await?;","+        Ok(())","+    }","+","     /// Build the auth state from the resolved config. A configured SQL","     /// backend backs both stores with one shared database; otherwise","     /// each local store is in-memory when its file path is unset and","@@ -306,6 +313,11 @@ pub trait UserBackend: Send + Sync {","     /// Remove `username`, reporting `false` when there is no such user. The","     /// user's tokens are not touched.","     async fn delete_user(&self, username: &str) -> Result<bool>;","+","+    /// Check that the user store backend is reachable and ready to process requests.","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        Ok(())","+    }"," }"," "," /// Bearer-token record store. The hot read is [`Self::lookup`]","@@ -313,6 +325,11 @@ pub trait UserBackend: Send + Sync {"," /// request); the rest back the `/-/npm/v1/tokens` CRUD endpoints."," #[async_trait]"," pub trait TokenBackend: Send + Sync {","+    /// Check that the token store backend is reachable and ready to process requests.","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        Ok(())","+    }","+","     /// Mint a fresh token for `username`, persist its hash, and return","     /// the raw token. The raw token is never stored.","     async fn issue(&self, username: &str) -> Result<String>;"],"additions":17,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/auth/src/libsql_backend.rs","lines":["@@ -185,6 +185,14 @@ impl LibsqlAuth {","         })","         .await","     }","+","+    async fn check_db_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        with_auth_timeout::<_, LibsqlError>(self.timeout, async {","+            self.conn.query(\"SELECT 1;\", ()).await?;","+            Ok(())","+        })","+        .await","+    }"," }"," "," #[async_trait]","@@ -217,6 +225,10 @@ impl UserBackend for LibsqlAuth {","     async fn delete_user(&self, username: &str) -> Result<bool> {","         self.remove_user(username).await","     }","+","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        self.check_db_readiness().await","+    }"," }"," "," impl LibsqlAuth {","@@ -452,6 +464,10 @@ impl TokenBackend for LibsqlAuth {","         self.conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM tokens WHERE token_hash = ?1\", params![key]).await?;","         Ok(Some(record))","     }","+","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        self.check_db_readiness().await","+    }"," }"," "," /// Decode a row selecting [`TOKEN_COLUMNS`] into its `(token_hash,"],"additions":16,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/auth/src/owned_tokens.rs","lines":["@@ -50,4 +50,8 @@ impl TokenBackend for OwnedTokens {","     async fn revoke_by_key(&self, key: &str) -> Result<Option<TokenRecord>> {","         self.tokens.revoke_by_key(key).await","     }","+","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        self.tokens.check_readiness().await","+    }"," }"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/auth/src/sqlx_backend.rs","lines":["@@ -83,6 +83,13 @@ impl<Db> SqlAuth<Db> {","         }","         self.db.reconcile_user_counter_overcount().await","     }","+","+    async fn check_db_readiness(&self) -> Result<()>","+    where","+        Db: AuthSqlBackend,","+    {","+        with_auth_timeout(self.timeout, self.db.check_readiness()).await","+    }"," }"," "," #[async_trait]","@@ -115,6 +122,9 @@ trait AuthSqlBackend: Send + Sync {","     async fn update_password_hash(&self, username: &str, bcrypt_hash: &str) -> Result<bool>;","     /// Remove the user and take one off the `users` counter in one transaction.","     async fn delete_user(&self, username: &str) -> Result<bool>;","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        Ok(())","+    }"," }"," "," #[derive(Clone)]","@@ -194,6 +204,10 @@ where","     async fn delete_user(&self, username: &str) -> Result<bool> {","         self.db.delete_user(username).await","     }","+","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        self.check_db_readiness().await","+    }"," }"," "," #[async_trait]","@@ -242,6 +256,10 @@ where","         self.db.delete_token(key).await?;","         Ok(Some(record))","     }","+","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        self.check_db_readiness().await","+    }"," }"," "," fn invalid_pool_size(backend: &str) -> RegistryError {"],"additions":18,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/auth/src/sqlx_backend/mysql.rs","lines":["@@ -241,6 +241,11 @@ impl AuthSqlBackend for MysqlDatabase {","         tx.commit().await?;","         Ok(removed > 0)","     }","+","+    async fn check_readiness(&self) -> Result<()> {","+        sqlx::query(\"SELECT 1;\").execute(&self.pool).await.map_err(RegistryError::from)?;","+        Ok(())","+    }"," }"," "," impl MysqlDatabase {"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/auth/sr